# This template is used by GitHub Actions to inject secrets from 1Password
# OP_VAULT is set dynamically by the workflow based on the branch (dev/prod)
DATABASE_URL="op://${OP_VAULT}/Database/connection_string"
SESSION_SECRET="op://${OP_VAULT}/App/session_secret"
# App's own public URL (86e2v1bbr) -- better-auth's baseURL. Same 1Password reference
# .env.post-deploy already uses for its health-check poll (established
# precedent, not invented here). Passed explicitly as `baseURL: process.env.APP_URL`
# in src/auth/better-auth.ts, so the env var name on the left does NOT need to
# match better-auth's own internal naming (e.g. BETTER_AUTH_URL) -- resolved at
# install time, confirmed working end-to-end against a real session round-trip.
# PREREQUISITE: this 1Password item is confirmed populated in the dev vault
# only -- a Production deploy needs the equivalent CapRover/app_url entry
# created in the prod vault first, or this line will fail the same way
# .env.post-deploy's own comment already flags for its copy.
APP_URL="op://${OP_VAULT}/CapRover/app_url"
# DEV_AUTH_HEADERS (86e2v1bbr): NOT a secret -- a plain boolean flag, not an
# op:// reference, so it's set directly rather than injected via 1Password.
# Set (e.g. "1") to trust the x-client-id/x-user-id dev headers directly (CI,
# local dev, the full-stack e2e suite -- see web/playwright.fullstack.config.ts
# -> package.json's dev:fullstack-server script). Unset (the default, and the
# CapRover Development/Production runtime env today) means a verified
# better-auth session is the ONLY accepted identity source -- a request
# bearing only the dev headers is rejected. Left unset here deliberately: the
# deployed Development dashboard has no login UI yet (86e2v1bdj) and no
# CapRover env override was added by this item, so setting it is a live
# security-exposure decision (86e2v24uf, parked on Bridge) this item does not
# make unilaterally -- see this item's PR for the full tradeoff.

